rganizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-14T02:59:25Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T03:03:33Z","body":"The bug should be fixed now. Basically, it is the issue fix of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103822 (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/2d4c32b3ae0a67620e8edbb4c9a68a2c13afdea4) was not wrong, but it does not consider the case of the `ShaderGraphEditor` since it also uses the same GraphNode class. However, because of the timing issue, the shader node cannot get the y position of the widget (it was so early that the value was still 0). But the GraphEditor widget app can achieve the position value at runtime. In this case, I separate the two cases using the `is_using_resort_layout` check.\n\nHere is the demo: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105370#issuecomment-2800345642\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions. Thanks!\ncc: @Chaosus @michaelharmonart @ASamBlur @ProgrammerOnCoffee \n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800349714/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2800356705","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105232#issuecomment-2800356705","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105232","id":2800356705,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m6g1h","user":{"login":"ytianle","id":61530469,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNTMwNDY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61530469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://